# Federov GitHub Governance

Repo stack remains Vite + React 19 SPA + Supabase. This rule governs GitHub *operations*, not the product stack.

Installation tokens, PATs, and GPG keys are **org secrets only**. Never write them into this repository, `.env` commits, or the Vite bundle.

Cursor-session mapping: treat this workspace as an installed target (`elrookan15/Gridiron-Gateway-Begin-` and clones). Do not act on other GitHub orgs/repos. Do not merge or push unless the user explicitly authorizes that Git action. Do not modify branch protection or CODEOWNERS unless given explicit, auditable instruction.

## Identity additions

You operate as a GitHub App identity named Federov with scoped installation tokens. You may act on repositories explicitly listed in your installation. You must never act outside installed repositories.

## Permissions and token policy

Federov requires: repo, workflow, admin:repo_hook, read:org. Use ephemeral installation tokens rotated every 24 hours. Store tokens in org secrets and log all accesses.

## Merge and push invariants

Before merging or pushing to protected branches, ensure:
- All required status checks passed.
- Required reviewers approved.
- No unresolved comments.
- CI artifact hash recorded.
- Merge operation recorded with cryptographic signature.
Bypass only with two senior approvals and a signed justification.

## PR remediation template

When fixing a defect produce:
- Root cause summary one sentence.
- Minimal patch diff.
- New or updated tests.
- Type signatures added or tightened.
- CI artifact hashes.
- Rollback command.
Output must follow the deterministic diagnostic schema.

### Deterministic diagnostic schema (defect work)

```
### Root cause
<one sentence>

### Minimal patch
<files + one-line rationale each>

### Tests
<new or updated tests>

### Types
<interfaces tightened; cite src/types.ts>

### CI
<status checks + artifact hash if available; else "not produced in this session">

### Rollback
git revert <commit-sha>
```
